duct 1. That is closest to true average demand, so this is likely the best.\n- **1** (every 3 days, 1.1×): similar totals (647 and 616). It pays fewer order fees but holds more product 1. Overflow risk is small.\n- **4** (every 2 days, 1.0×): slightly short on both products, but low holding cost. For product 1 it probably beats over-ordering.\n- **2** (product 0 at 1.0×, product 1 at 1.2×): it over-orders product 1 by roughly 90 units and pays to hold the excess. Borderline for the top half.\n- **0** (every 3 days, 1.2×) and **7** (1.25×): systematic over-ordering. For candidate 7 the excess product 0 alone is about 118 units, or roughly 1,060 spoiled. Candidate 0 can also overflow the warehouse on days 14 and 23.\n- **3** (every 4 days): high product 1 holding cost and repeated overflow. For example, on about day 13 roughly 210 units arrive against 188 places.\n- **5** (orders every day): 26 order fees (about 1,170). It also has no safety stock, so shortages cost an estimated 1,500."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5068, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5068}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:18:02.260Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWCQbToJVMXjh6XUJEeH"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01YZLsVDVGiKGtuDqBGCTDrR", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "m